{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Stores","title":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"Persistence","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"Persistence","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker(store:)"},{"type":"text","text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":". A segment is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps every event type declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the program’s modules, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s own; ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore(events:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps only the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types it lists. Each record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"date in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type of your own or in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types, such as one that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run but never written, and reported once as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drop is reported on "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"type":"text","text":": the oldest segments"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at another "},{"code":"schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set. Call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":", after the tracker’s "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"GRDBPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"abstract":[{"text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","title":"DropReport","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notPersisted"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","abstract":[{"text":"A record of the event named ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","title":"SegmentStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","type":"topic","title":"synchronize()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"synchronize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage (","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so it survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence","title":"Persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","title":"RecordStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","fragments"